From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Wang <jimwan@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 17:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] configure: support sanitized kernel headers

The Yocto recipe passes --with-sanitized-headers so display interface headers
are checked against the staged kernel UAPI. Define the option in configure and
add the requested directory to CPPFLAGS, making the dependency explicit for
linux-qcom-next 7.x based builds.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Jim Wang <jimwan@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 configure.ac | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 40ae6eb..426038f 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -21,6 +21,20 @@ AC_SUBST([AM_CPPFLAGS], [--std=c++11])
 AC_PROG_CC
 AM_PROG_CC_C_O
 AC_PROG_CXX
+
+AC_ARG_WITH([sanitized-headers],
+  [AS_HELP_STRING([--with-sanitized-headers=DIR],
+    [path to staged sanitized kernel headers])],
+  [sanitized_headers="$withval"],
+  [sanitized_headers=""])
+
+AS_IF([test "x$sanitized_headers" != "x" && test "x$sanitized_headers" != "xno"], [
+  AS_IF([test ! -d "$sanitized_headers"], [
+    AC_MSG_ERROR([sanitized kernel header path does not exist: $sanitized_headers])
+  ])
+  CPPFLAGS="$CPPFLAGS -I$sanitized_headers"
+])
+
 AC_PROG_LIBTOOL
 AC_PROG_AWK
 AC_PROG_CPP
-- 
2.34.1
